{"id":"023e15d0-5f8e-448d-bb7a-ca9a25b1d4e5","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"4f098256bcabad51","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/catalog.ts","baseline":{"blob":"9c8753998a23e45e509f1074aeb8d9470586109a","start":3322,"end":3348},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","captured","\"",":","(",")","=>","boolean",";"]},"context":{"before":"35e03684ac67ec4e","after":"7e5424d3e347db43"}},"payload":{"text":"Whether the statement running goes into a pipe or a file (session.ts `outputCaptured`): then a streaming command\nhands its output back through the shell instead of writing it live.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:54.796Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:54.796Z"}
{"id":"07955405-4f82-4e7b-9943-3cc3ed8d74ad","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"ab4a8f5ce508f3ab","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/catalog.ts","baseline":{"blob":"cc7d60507d9a4349768ef988872ab7fa0de22161","start":3759,"end":3819},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","history","\"",":","{","\"","lines","\"",":","(",")","=>","string","[]",";","\"","clear","\"",":","(",")","=>","void","}",";"]},"context":{"before":"510ee8c1730ae5df","after":"b3836412d3627918"}},"payload":{"text":"The lines this terminal's run: what ↑ goes back through (`history`).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:52.069Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:52.069Z"}
{"id":"0ebac865-d6d4-4acd-87c7-2749cecf76cb","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"10798977cec13a9e","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/catalog.ts","baseline":{"blob":"bd2869ff460ff886ccf9c02070ccb7068e3dd5f4","start":2334,"end":2353},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","notHere","\"","?",":","string",";"]},"context":{"before":"61d02e94992a2eb1","after":"f69159af0dff270b"}},"payload":{"text":"It isn't here, and this says what to do instead: its whole folder is this file, and whatever it's given, it says so.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:57.926Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:57.926Z"}
{"id":"12bbc851-a437-4b10-8814-2bd07d73a6b7","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a4eb2d27eddc588a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/catalog.ts","baseline":{"blob":"cbfc75a02e8d8bf5481b41b6bda96240e9bd7352","start":38,"end":84},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Hub","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/hub","\""]},"context":{"after":"0b97702791607673"}},"payload":{"text":"The terminal's own commands, found rather than listed: each is a folder under `commands/`, named after the command,\nholding everything about it — `command.ts` (what it is: its name, a line saying what it does, whether it streams),\n`<name>.ts` (the implementation, loaded the first time the command runs) and its tests. Adding a command is adding a\nfolder; everything that enumerates commands derives from here — tab completion and which commands make a line run a\nstatement at a time (session.ts) — so neither is a list to keep up by hand. What isn't here is just-bash's \"not\nfound\", or, for what someone's likely to try, a folder saying what to do instead (`notHere`). The terminal is people's; an agent's way in is a tool (app/tools/host.ts).\n\nOnly `command.ts` is read here, eagerly — it's a few lines and imports nothing — so anything can ask what the\ncommands are without loading a command (index.ts loads the implementations, lazily).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:03:03.719Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:03:03.719Z"}
{"id":"17f1d9b5-d8e5-4293-9b6c-820bc731b3c8","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"510ee8c1730ae5df","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/catalog.ts","baseline":{"blob":"5fe38883fb4b4536fe42dd04a80915845078624d","start":3641,"end":3679},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","session","\"",":","(",")","=>","Promise","<","BashSession",">",";"]},"context":{"before":"7e5424d3e347db43","after":"ab4a8f5ce508f3ab"}},"payload":{"text":"The shell itself, to run a line in (`npm run` runs its script there).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:53.385Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:53.385Z"}
{"id":"4d424645-23c8-4757-9add-a6876e986720","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"61d02e94992a2eb1","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/catalog.ts","baseline":{"blob":"efc07ce7aea84dddc12c3e61773d32a54f144846","start":2078,"end":2100},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","streaming","\"","?",":","boolean",";"]},"context":{"before":"c563e35e7558c5e3","after":"10798977cec13a9e"}},"payload":{"text":"Its output goes to the terminal as it's produced rather than through just-bash's stdout (node) — or it runs\nlines that may (npm): a line with it runs a statement at a time, so what came before shows first (session.ts).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:59.139Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:59.139Z"}
{"id":"7d579c3d-1a6f-4767-8879-79e16d5bbc1a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"5b282a2ca826538b#0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/catalog.ts","baseline":{"blob":"2c2779a1e67facac8b115cd7209b9729ad9d6fa7","start":1460,"end":1478},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","summary","\"",":","string",";"]},"context":{"before":"9794d7b0607f5d34","after":"5b235e5ffa42fadc#0"}},"payload":{"text":"What it does, in a line: shown in `--help`.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:03:01.807Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:03:01.807Z"}
{"id":"7eed7051-10d7-407f-a994-6d9d9004f675","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"e4217438b814ddec","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/catalog.ts","baseline":{"blob":"15700caf6f69e4e3a8d21a9e4eb26e021ca1bfaa","start":4372,"end":4438},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","type","CommandFactory","=","(","host",":","CommandHost",")","=>","Implementation"]},"context":{"before":"8a1fd28898982677","after":"85ceac39dd5275d7"}},"payload":{"text":"A command's implementation module: its `<name>.ts` exports `create`.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:51.351Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:51.351Z"}
{"id":"8b1fd28a-ae04-4cea-ba3f-b9015485aa68","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"5c87c91396a5a066","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/catalog.ts","baseline":{"blob":"1894843ba3951e55403e6ec43dba7dcfb4c00c77","start":2777,"end":2797},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","numberIs","\"","?",":","string",";"]},"context":{"before":"e3b57437ec53ae63","after":"315dcb3eb4beb853"}},"payload":{"text":"The option a bare `-<number>` gives, as git's `-3` is `-n 3` (`git log -3`): juvy knows no such flag.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:56.717Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:56.717Z"}
{"id":"9217ce66-deba-4b66-8411-414c06efbf21","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2c5d685d43fd1fa9#0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/catalog.ts","baseline":{"blob":"62a94b1b3605cd5e8992b4a63c2eeaf224602b69","start":1728,"end":1750},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","stopEarly","\"","?",":","boolean",";"]},"context":{"before":"5b235e5ffa42fadc#0","after":"c563e35e7558c5e3"}},"payload":{"text":"Parse only up to the first argument: it and everything after it are passed on as they are — a command that runs\nanother (`node app.ts --port 3`).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:03:00.567Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:03:00.567Z"}
{"id":"b0805135-7efa-4b0e-bd62-db6a336a8083","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"5b235e5ffa42fadc#0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/catalog.ts","baseline":{"blob":"308dda02373fe46aadf9dfeaec461f26a972a440","start":1532,"end":1551},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","options","\"","?",":","Schema",";"]},"context":{"before":"5b282a2ca826538b#0","after":"2c5d685d43fd1fa9#0"}},"payload":{"text":"Its options and arguments, as a juvy schema: juvy parses them (strictly), validates them and makes `--help` of\nthem, so the command gets them parsed (invoke.ts).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:03:01.197Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:03:01.197Z"}
{"id":"bbe26635-681c-495b-a9b7-2b42b3aefbf1","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"9794d7b0607f5d34","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/catalog.ts","baseline":{"blob":"900e205cd99d27a039b8533339ec8d89ff74a209","start":1397,"end":1412},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","name","\"",":","string",";"]},"context":{"before":"66f77736674fa3ad#0","after":"5b282a2ca826538b#0"}},"payload":{"text":"The command's name, and its folder's.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:03:02.503Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:03:02.503Z"}
{"id":"bd5e037b-152c-4cbe-84f8-a30c61231d17","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"c563e35e7558c5e3","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/catalog.ts","baseline":{"blob":"155eb58269ccb9575fbc7941ca1a9b78b00488a4","start":1911,"end":1964},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","subcommands","\"","?",":","Record","<","string",",","SubcommandDefinition",">",";"]},"context":{"before":"2c5d685d43fd1fa9#0","after":"61d02e94992a2eb1"}},"payload":{"text":"In place of `options`, its subcommands (`git status`), each with its own — routed, and helped, by juvy.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:59.868Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:59.868Z"}
{"id":"cc7c8c8a-6ed6-42d6-90ed-63754a9c7980","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"35e03684ac67ec4e","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/catalog.ts","baseline":{"blob":"6b72c58a8717420a24d23c85bd27d268f464c026","start":3226,"end":3250},"shape":{"type":"PropertySignature","atoms":["\"","writeLive","\"",":","NodeOutput",";"]},"context":{"before":"a5263b5b92d2dca4","after":"4f098256bcabad51"}},"payload":{"text":"Write to this terminal now, as it's produced (stderr in red).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:55.427Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:55.427Z"}
{"id":"eb37c4af-2983-4168-8aed-caa2710572d5","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"3a5bdb617872e36f","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/catalog.ts","baseline":{"blob":"23aba2b020d9857b248b339d845312ca6720cea5","start":1298,"end":1566},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","interface","CommandDefinition","{","\"","name","\"",":","string",";","\"","summary","\"",":","string",";","\"","options","\"","?",":","Schema",";","\"","stopEarly","\"","?",":","boolean",";","\"","subcommands","\"","?",":","Record","<","string",",","SubcommandDefinition",">",";","\"","streaming","\"","?",":","boolean",";","\"","notHere","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","subcommandsNotHere","\"","?",":","Record","<","string",",","string",">",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"0560722224125b65","after":"a3b3ff07e6cd7289"}},"payload":{"text":"What a command is: its `command.ts`'s default export.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:03:03.099Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:03:03.099Z"}
